.TH STORAGE-MAP 1 "2026" "storage-map" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
storage-map \- see what fills a drive and clean it up
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B storage-map
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Storage Map shows the contents of a drive as a treemap and lists large files,
duplicates, old files, caches and build folders. Without options it opens its
user interface in a browser window.
.PP
Scans read names, sizes and dates. Files are only read during a duplicate search.
Nothing is removed without confirmation, and system folders are protected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-scan " PATH"
Scan without a user interface and add the result to the history.
.TP
.B \-\-mcp
Run as a Model Context Protocol server over stdio. Access is read-only until
changed in the user interface.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
Do not open a window, print the address instead.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " N"
Use a fixed port. The default is 47811.
.TP
.BI \-\-token " T"
Use a fixed access token instead of a random one.
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-dir " PATH"
Keep scans, history and settings in this folder.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Show invented drives. Nothing is read or deleted.
.TP
.BI \-\-demo\-scale " N"
Demo with N times as many files.
.TP
.BI \-\-sandbox " PATH"
Real scan and cleanup, limited to this test folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-make\-fixture " DIR"
Create a test folder with known contents.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/storage-map/
Scans, history and the log of MCP calls. Follows XDG_DATA_HOME.
.TP
.I ~/.config/storage-map/config.json
Settings. Follows XDG_CONFIG_HOME.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project page: https://github.com/codeflag/storage-map
